      "content": "While 5-HTP is often considered a safer alternative for hormonal users, it still carries risks of drug interactions, particularly with certain antidepressants commonly prescribed alongside birth control. Vitamin D, although generally safe, does not directly impact birth control effectiveness but may require testing if you have widespread fatigue or other deficiencies unrelated to your mood. Given your current situation and the need for safe, reliable support, I strongly recommend discussing these specific options with a licensed pharmacist who can review your full medication history before you start anything new. Please prioritize your safety by avoiding unverified online advice and sticking to guidance from a medical professional to prevent any adverse health outcomes.",
